Package: geant4
Version: @VERSION@-@REVISION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: libc6, libstdc++6, libexpat1, zlib1g, ca-certificates, debconf (>= 0.5) | debconf-2.0,
 libxerces-c3.2t64 | libxerces-c3.2, libgl1, libglu1-mesa, libxmu6,
 libqt6core6t64 | libqt6core6, libqt6gui6t64 | libqt6gui6, libqt6widgets6t64 | libqt6widgets6,
 libqt6opengl6t64 | libqt6opengl6, libqt6openglwidgets6t64 | libqt6openglwidgets6
Recommends: curl | wget
Maintainer: Ovidio Peña Rodríguez <ovidio@bytesfall.com>
Homepage: https://geant4.web.cern.ch/
Description: Toolkit for the simulation of the passage of particles through matter
 Geant4 is a toolkit for simulating the passage of particles through matter,
 covering geometry, tracking, the physics of the interactions and the
 bookkeeping around them.  This package carries the libraries, the headers
 and the tools of Geant4 @VERSION@, installed under @PREFIX@.
 .
 The data files are not in the package.  Installation asks which of them are
 wanted and downloads them from cern.ch, checking each against the MD5 that
 geant4-config records.  Seven of the twelve are preselected: those are the
 ones Geant4 turns into a fatal exception the moment it builds its physics
 tables, so without them nothing will run.  The rest can be added at any time
 with @PREFIX@/share/Geant4/fetch-datasets.sh.
 .
 This is not the official Geant4 distribution; it is a build with the Qt6
 user interface, packaged to install the same way on all three platforms.
